00:12:38.839 --> 00:12:44.599
University of California Riverside researchers Therunia Yogananda and Wantong Lee, semiconductor

00:12:44.599 --> 00:12:49.519
engineering reports, published a paper on splitting the high bandwidth memory controller

00:12:49.519 --> 00:12:55.059
between the host and the memory-based die, which recent stacks such as HBM4 can build

00:12:55.059 --> 00:12:56.139
on a logic process.

00:12:57.102 --> 00:13:03.622
A training step on a consumer GPU comes apart at the copy, and infer.bia.ai times that copy

00:13:03.622 --> 00:13:04.622
against the arithmetic.

00:13:05.262 --> 00:13:12.622
The guide rates in RTX 4090 at 82.6 teraflops of BF16, then names three gaps the flops

00:13:12.622 --> 00:13:20.682
do not close, 24GB of memory against 80, a link of 32GB per second against 900, and no

00:13:20.682 --> 00:13:23.202
error correcting memory where training expects it.

00:13:23.202 --> 00:13:28.222
Wates, optimizer state, and activations all have to fit in those 24GB.

00:13:28.982 --> 00:13:33.602
If the model is split across cards, a slice of those numbers has to move after every

00:13:33.602 --> 00:13:33.902
layer.

00:13:34.622 --> 00:13:36.442
PCI expresses the only path.

00:13:37.002 --> 00:13:42.642
There is no NV link, so a tensor parallel all-reduce cannot hide on a dedicated GPU fabric.

00:13:43.262 --> 00:13:48.002
Take the guide's 7 billion parameter case, shard it across 8 of those cards.

00:13:48.002 --> 00:13:55.202
MicroBatch of 1, Sequence Length 2048, Full Check Pointing, Activations are about 2

00:13:55.202 --> 00:13:58.902
Gigabytes, The Running Total about 18, and The Headroom 6.

00:13:59.702 --> 00:14:02.382
That 6 Gigabytes is the budget for a longer sequence.

00:14:02.902 --> 00:14:08.622
At 4,096 tokens, the same card needs gradient checkpointing, and a MicroBatch of 1.

00:14:09.242 --> 00:14:13.762
Longer context is the memory left after weights and optimizer state have taken their share.

00:14:13.762 --> 00:14:17.482
The wire is why more cards do not refill that budget.

00:14:18.102 --> 00:14:21.402
Tensor parallel all reduce has to finish after every layer.

00:14:22.002 --> 00:14:28.582
The guide times it at 640 milliseconds on PCI Express and 22 milliseconds on NV link.

00:14:29.102 --> 00:14:34.922
If the forward and backward pass takes 500 milliseconds, the PCI Express copy more than

00:14:34.922 --> 00:14:35.762
doubles the step.

00:14:36.382 --> 00:14:41.502
Fully sharded data parallel does not dodge the bus, and all gather at the start of each

00:14:41.502 --> 00:14:47.542
layer and a reduced scatter at the end add about 900 milliseconds on PCI express to a 7 billion

00:14:47.542 --> 00:14:54.002
parameter step that would spend about 32 milliseconds on the fast link. 8 cards by 8 small

00:14:54.002 --> 00:14:58.722
memories and a bus that spends longer synchronizing than the arithmetic spends computing.

00:14:59.322 --> 00:15:02.942
The cluster stops being the right machine when either budget is spent.

00:15:03.682 --> 00:15:08.822
Once sequence length eats the six gigabytes of headroom, another card does not make one larger

00:15:08.822 --> 00:15:09.582
address space.

00:15:10.242 --> 00:15:16.322
Once the 640 millisecond all reduce outlasts the 500 millisecond compute step, another

00:15:16.322 --> 00:15:18.662
card joins the copy instead of shortening it.

00:15:19.322 --> 00:15:22.122
The 82.6 Teraflops are still on the board.

00:15:22.702 --> 00:15:28.142
They wait on 32 GB per second and on 24 GB that cannot see the next 24.

